      {
        "id": "intro",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Shape a Mix with a Three-Band EQ\n\nSynthesizes a bass line under a noise bed and shapes it with the four biquad filters. Every step runs in the editor process, with no file, model or key.\n\n**How it works:** \"1 Source\" is a Code node that writes a bass line and soft noise. \"2 Rumble\" is a high-pass at 40 Hz. \"3 Lows\" boosts below 120 Hz, \"4 Mids\" cuts 2.5 kHz and \"5 Air\" lifts above 8 kHz. \"6 Limit\" keeps the boosted signal under -1 dB. \"Dry level\" passes the source to \"Before\" at 0 dB. Compare \"Before\" with \"After\".\n\n**Try this:** Set Gain dB on \"4 Mids\" to +6 to hear the harsh band, or move its frequency."
        },
        "ui_properties": {
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
          },
          "zIndex": 0,
          "width": 640,
          "selectable": true,
          "height": 300
        },
        "dynamic_properties": {},
        "dynamic_outputs": {}
      },
      {
        "id": "src",
        "type": "nodetool.code.Code",
        "data": {
          "code": "// Four seconds of a bass line (root, fifth, octave) over soft white noise.\nconst rate = 44100, seconds = 4;\nconst line = [55, 82.41, 110, 82.41];\nconst samples = new Float32Array(rate * seconds);\nlet seed = 11;\nconst noise = () => { seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296; return seed / 2147483648 - 1; };\nfor (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) {\n  const t = i / rate;\n  const beat = Math.floor(t * 2);\n  const u = t - beat / 2;\n  const freq = line[beat % line.length];\n  const bass = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * freq * t) * Math.exp(-3 * u);\n  samples[i] = 0.4 * bass + 0.08 * noise();\n}\n\n// 16-bit PCM WAV bytes from interleaved samples in [-1, 1].\nfunction wav(samples, rate, channels) {\n  const bytes = new Uint8Array(44 + samples.length * 2);\n  const view = new DataView(bytes.buffer);\n  const tag = (at, text) => { for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) bytes[at + i] = text.charCodeAt(i); };\n  tag(0, \"RIFF\"); view.setUint32(4, 36 + samples.length * 2, true); tag(8, \"WAVE\");\n  tag(12, \"fmt \"); view.setUint32(16, 16, true); view.setUint16(20, 1, true);\n  view.setUint16(22, channels, true); view.setUint32(24, rate, true);\n  view.setUint32(28, rate * channels * 2, true); view.setUint16(32, channels * 2, true);\n  view.setUint16(34, 16, true); tag(36, \"data\"); view.setUint32(40, samples.length * 2, true);\n  samples.forEach((s, i) => view.setInt16(44 + i * 2, Math.round(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, s)) * 32767), true));\n  return bytes;\n}\n\nawait output(\"audio\", await media.toAudio(wav(samples, rate, 1), { mimeType: \"audio/wav\", filename: \"source.wav\" }));\n"
        },
